[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Not Enough Waypoints[/b] adds six waypoints to Baldur's Gate 3, in the places you keep walking back to.

The game puts most of its waypoints at the edge of a place: outside the Emerald Grove, outside the goblin camp's temple, outside Moonrise Towers. The traders, quest givers and doors you need are often a long walk further in. These six waypoints stand where that walk is longest.

Each one is built the way the game builds its own in that kind of place: in buildings and against them, the game's waypoint rune on a wall; in the open, the rune on a boulder like the one at the Blighted Village. They work like the game's own too: walk near one to unlock it, then travel to it from the map or any other waypoint.[/color][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]The Hollow[/b] (Act 1): a boulder on the floor of the Hollow in the Emerald Grove, against the ledge below Okta's and Auntie Ethel's stalls, across from Dammon's forge.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Underdark - Arcane Tower[/b] (Act 1): the rune on the tower's wall, a few steps from its front door.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Shattered Sanctum[/b] (Act 1): inside the goblin camp's temple, the rune on the wall by the pillar east of the spider pits, between Dror Ragzlin's throne room, Minthara and True Soul Gut.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Moonrise Towers - Main Floor[/b] (Act 2): the rune on a wall of the main floor, east of the bazaar.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Open Hand Temple[/b] (Act 3): a boulder in the street in front of the temple in Rivington, where the refugees beg.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Guildhall[/b] (Act 3): the rune on the wall beside the bar in the main hall, where Nine-Fingers Keene's visitors wait.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Every waypoint was placed with the game's own navigation data and checked against everything the game puts nearby, its sub-levels and how far each object reaches included. If one still floats, clips into something or stands in the way, please report it on the Bugs tab or on [url=https://github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/NotEnoughWaypoints/issues/new/choose]GitHub[/url], with a screenshot.

[b]New in 1.1:[/b] five of the six waypoints moved to where they were meant to be. The Guildhall, Moonrise Towers, the Arcane Tower and the Shattered Sanctum are now the rune on a wall, as the game does in and against buildings, and the Open Hand Temple stands in the street in front of the temple. Saves made with 1.0 are moved too. The new places pass every check of the tools but have not been seen in game yet.

Open source (MIT): [url=https://github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/NotEnoughWaypoints]github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/NotEnoughWaypoints[/url][/color][/size]

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Install this mod with your mod manager:[/color]
[/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]BG3 Mod Manager[/b]: import the zip, move [i]Not Enough Waypoints[/i] to the active list, then save and export the load order.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Vortex[/b]: install, enable, deploy.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Manual[/b]: put [i]NotEnoughWaypoints.pak[/i] in [i]%LOCALAPPDATA%\Larian Studios\Baldur's Gate 3\Mods[/i] and enable it in your mod manager.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Load a save and walk to one of the places above.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]It works in a new game and in an existing save. When an update moves a waypoint, it is moved in your save too.
Removing it in the middle of a playthrough is not recommended: once a save has the waypoints, they are part of its story. The save still loads without the mod (the game warns that a mod is missing), but waypoints you unlocked may stay on the map without working.[/color][/size]

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Six new waypoints[/b] across all three acts, where the nearest one is a long walk away.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Built like the game's own[/b]: in buildings and against them, the rune on a wall, turned and raised like the game's own wall runes; in the open, a copy of the Blighted Village boulder and rune, in a colour that suits the place. Unlocked the same way.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]They follow the story[/b]: each is locked with the rest of its act when the story moves on, like the game's own. The Hollow is also locked when the druids seal the Emerald Grove, together with the game's Grove waypoint, so it never gets you past the barrier.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Sovereign Glut comes along[/b]: the Arcane Tower counts as an Underdark waypoint, so he follows the party there.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Placed with the game's own data[/b]: every rune sits on a wall measured from the game's own tiles, or on a boulder resting on free floor from the game's navigation grid, clear of everything the game puts there, with room for the whole party in front. Nothing is a guessed coordinate.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Nothing replaced[/b]: the mod adds its own objects, one small story script and the waypoint names. It replaces none of the game's files.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Multiplayer[/b]: waypoints unlock for the whole party, as usual.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Baldur's Gate 3 Patch 8. The waypoints are placed and checked against the Patch 8 Hotfix 10 game files.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]No other mods.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]The waypoint names are in English only for now.[/color][/size]

